 """Fearless draft flags, inferred from the drafts.
 
 In Fearless draft a champion picked in one game of a series cannot be picked again in that series.
-Leaguepedia has no format field, so the format is inferred per tournament:
-  1. A multi-game series is Fearless-looking if no champion is picked twice across its games.
-  2. A tournament is Fearless if at least 90% of its multi-game series are Fearless-looking.
-  3. Tournaments with only single-game series count as standard.
-Every game takes its tournament's flag.
+Leaguepedia has no format field, so the format is inferred per tournament from three series tests:
+  hard   no champion is picked twice across the series, by either team;
+  reset  the hard test on every game except the series' last one (Fearless with a reset decider,
+         where game 3 of a Bo3 or game 5 of a Bo5 resets the draft or is blind pick);
+  soft   no team picks the same champion twice in the series (Leaguepedia also calls this Fearless).
+A tournament is Fearless if at least 90% of its tested series pass any one test. The reset test needs
+at least 3 series with 3 or more games, and the soft test at least 5 multi-game series.
+Tournaments with only single-game series count as standard. Every game takes its tournament's flag.
 """
 
 import pandas as pd
 
 THRESHOLD = 0.9
+MIN_RESET_SERIES = 3
+MIN_SOFT_SERIES = 5
 
 
+def _multi_game(games: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:
+    n_games = games.groupby("match_id")["game_id"].transform("size")
+    return games[n_games >= 2]
+
+
 def series_fearless(games: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.Series:
-    """1.0 or 0.0 per multi-game series (match_id); series with one game are left out."""
